dquartered in Iselin, New Jersey.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Nadine M. Duchemin-Leslie | President, CEO & Chairman of the Board | Age 62 | Compensation: $1.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 395 people. Revenue per employee of $493K ranks in the bottom quartile among Utilities peers. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Middlesex Water Company is a small-cap utilities business with a $1.1B market cap on $195M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 5% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and interest coverage runs at 3.8\u00d7.","Net dilution runs at 0.5% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 2.3% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 66% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6552657258219966},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Regulatory rate-case risk and rising cost of capital \u2014 the allowed return is set by commissions, and the business lives or dies by that negotiation.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Grid modernisation capex burden \u2014 aging infrastructure requires massive reinvestment that regulators may not fully allow into rate base, compressing earned returns.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Wildfire and climate liability \u2014 extreme weather events create catastrophic, uninsurable losses that can push even investment-grade utilities toward restructuring.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 durability is the real test of a moat","39 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Price-Driven Insight from (MSEX) for Rule-Based Strategy","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/134/Price-Driven_Insight_from_MSEX_for_Rule-Based_Strategy_111226022202_1794511322.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794511322.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is Earnings Growth Altering The Investment Case For Middlesex Water Stock (MSEX)?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/utilities/nasdaq-msex/middlesex-water/news/is-earnings-growth-altering-the-investment-case-for-middlese","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794226752.7,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.743,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"3 Water Utility Stocks for Steady Income. One Has Raised Dividends for 54 Years","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/3-water-utility-stocks-steady-181740000.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794594473.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.643,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"\u201cBitter Christmas\u201d Is Pedro Almodvar\u2019s Gift to Us","source":"newyorker.com","link":"https://www.newyorker.com/culture/the-current-cinema/bitter-christmas-is